00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:04.850
<i>What should we do?</i>
<i>We're not used to facing adversity</i>

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:09.980
<i>So our resolve's definitely not all there</i>

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.400
<i>Back then, we were just</i>

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.730
<i>Envious of others and</i>

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:19.440
<i>Angry at something we couldn't see</i>

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.980
<i>We just kept glaring at the next step</i>

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.350
<i>That we could've easily taken</i>

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:29.310
<i>And it was eating away at us silently</i>

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:33.150
<i>We were so scared that we went numb</i>

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.560
<i>And our legs buckled from under us</i>

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:40.440
<i>We still can't forget the tears</i>
<i>that fell back then even now</i>

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:45.230
<i>Even though we're so frail we might break,</i>
<i>we still continued to seek love</i>

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:50.350
<i>We don't want to forget the reason</i>
<i>we're standing on this stage</i>

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:55.150
<i>Because you're the one who made me stronger</i>

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:59.600
<i>I give you this lovely ballad</i>
<i>within this beautiful attack</i>

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.900
So you're just wandering around with a snack?

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.770
Must be nice.

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:18.310
Could you at least act like you feel bad?

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:21.100
We might not go to the
Spring Tournament because of you.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.940
I know that.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:26.230
This is the seniors' last year, so I feel bad.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:28.810
But I didn't do anything wrong.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:33.020
It's not just the seniors.
We're also losing a chance!

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.350
You know, you seem really obsessed
with the Spring Tournament.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:40.560
Why don't you just go back to your
old school in Tokyo if you love it so much?

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.980
H-Hey. Where are you going?

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.600
I'm going back to Tokyo.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.150
Huh?

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:57.310
I'm going back to Meisei Academy.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:00.300
Episode 5: 'S t a n d   B y   M e'

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.900
Wouldn't me leaving the prefecture
without telling anyone

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:05.150
while people think I was
involved in some scandal

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.560
make me look worse?

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.650
This is all your fault to begin with.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.190
I mean...

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:17.150
It's my cousin. Oh, the one that's not Yori.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:20.100
Apparently your whole family's difficult.

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:23.150
You're not gonna answer?

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.190
Well, I sorta got in a fight with her.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:27.650
Oh, it stopped.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.850
If you're so worried about it, call them back.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.350
Nah, it's fine.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:40.150
But, Haijima... You aren't actually going
to fill out transfer papers, are you?

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:41.440
Who knows?

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.060
Really?

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:47.230
Maybe something will change if I see Sota.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:48.690
Sota?

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:51.150
Sota Yoshino.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.270
My volleyball buddy since the fourth grade.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:59.690
So, uh... Is Sota the one who attempted suicide?

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:00.940
Yeah.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.810
We were in a local club in grade school.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:10.310
The coach there, Ms. Minami,
told me about Meisei.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:14.350
We all promised we'd go to the
Spring Tournament from Meisei,

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:16.350
so I applied for Meisei.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:19.150
Y'all sound like you get along fine so far.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:23.020
I don't know about now, though.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:26.440
And then, at Meisei Middle School...

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:30.270
What? Hospital?

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:33.150
They found him at home and he...

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:37.020
I guess rumors like that spread like wildfire.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:42.440
I got called a murderer and
all kinds of other things and bullied.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.230
We will be arriving in Hamamatsu shortly.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.020
I quit going to school during the second term,

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.520
and then transferred over here our third term.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:50.350
And, well, you know the rest.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:53.100
Haijima...

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:56.560
Tokyo. Tokyo.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.650
Maybe you shouldn't go after all.

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:02.980
Nothing good's gonna come from you
coming back to a place like that.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:05.020
You're the one who egged me on.

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:07.310
You're the one who told me to go back to Tokyo.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:11.400
That's just because you said...

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.520
You better take responsibility for this.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:22.190
Because... I might chicken out.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:26.980
Wow, this is like one of those schools
you see in some TV drama!

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:30.770
We sure got in easy since it's spring break...

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:32.060
Kuroba.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:35.020
I think... I might be nervous.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.770
Haijima, you're not turning back, are you?

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:43.600
You knew what you were getting into.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.480
I egged you on, remember?

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.690
I'm not gonna give you an escape route.
You're okay with that, aren't you?

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:02.600
There're four courts here! It's huge!

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:05.350
Meisei puts a lot of money
into their sports programs.

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:08.230
I don't see the volleyball team.
Are they practicing outside?

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:09.940
Huh? Chika?

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.480
Whoa, it actually is Chika.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.350
Tetto... Kou...

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.230
The second and third years
are off doing practice matches

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:27.400
and then we have practice at 4 PM.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:30.650
Oh, yeah. Where'd you transfer to again?

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.230
Was it the Tohoku region?

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:34.310
It's the Hokuriku region, not Tohoku.

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:36.520
Seiin High in Fukui.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.020
Is that your friend from there?

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.440
That's Kuroba, one of my high school teammates.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.270
And my friend since kindergarten.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.900
And he's our ace spiker.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.400
Huh...

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.850
He's a first year, right?

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:51.230
That's pretty impressive. Oh, I'm Komukai and...

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:53.310
Hello, I'm Ikawa.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:56.980
Seiin from Fukui? Never heard of it.
Do you have a pretty strong team?

00:07:56.980 --> 00:08:00.310
We don't have much of a track
record yet, but that'll change.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:02.150
I see.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:07.230
We went to the Kanto Tournament this year,
but couldn't get past the top 16.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:09.730
But that's because of the older team members.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.980
Did you have anything to do with it?

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:15.900
I see you haven't changed.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.650
What do you mean?

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.520
I think it's pretty obvious.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:23.150
More importantly, is that
Yoshino kid here today?

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:25.900
Yoshino? You mean Sota Yoshino?

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:30.270
Sota quit volleyball and transferred schools.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.520
He quit volleyball?

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:36.190
Wait... Did he quit because of that?

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:37.400
"That"?

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.480
You know, the thing that happened with Sota.

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:42.440
The thing? Oh, right.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:46.480
I'm surprised. I didn't think you'd
still be worried about that, Chika.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:50.190
I can say this now, can't I, Kou?
Sota's not here anymore anyway.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:53.690
We knew how dense Chika was, but we figured

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:57.480
that he'd adjust his attitude
if someone actually died.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:02.900
So we joked and said someone should
actually say they did and Sota volunteered.

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:07.270
I mean, even we were shocked
when he actually pulled it off, but--

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.270
What the hell?!

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:10.400
You guys really can't tell the difference
between something awful and a joke?!

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:12.600
Y-You've got nothing to do with this!

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.350
It's not like we thought Chika would
transfer over something like that.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:18.520
"Something like that"?

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:21.560
The hell's this guy's problem? Hey, Chika.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:29.310
Haijima!

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:39.520
Haijima...

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:43.100
There's no reason for you guys
to play volleyball like them.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.940
You're going to play volleyball with Seiin.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:50.270
Seiin along with Captain Oda,
Aoki- <i>senpai</i> , and Kanno- <i>senpai</i> .

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.980
Coming to Tokyo was a great idea!

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:59.560
Now we know how shitty these guys are,
so you've got nothing to worry about!

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:01.690
If you play volleyball--

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:03.810
H-Hey, Haijima?

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:04.980
Haijima!

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.960
[Setter] The command tower of the team
and the player who sets the ball to the 
spikers. They're expected to set balls easy for 
spikers to hit and to 
adjust messy bumps.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.850
Where am I...?

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:30.400
Hey... You're awake?

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.060
Sota?

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:38.100
Kou sent me a message, so I came.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.730
I see...

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:43.400
Hey, Sota.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.350
Did you really quit volleyball...?

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:48.850
Why?

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:53.650
Ever since we got into middle school,
I really wanted to quit.

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:56.310
But we all made that promise,

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:58.770
so I couldn't say I wanted to back out.

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:01.980
My mom was in the PTA, too.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:05.900
A lot of things tied me down,
and I couldn't breathe.

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.150
So...

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:10.730
I figured if it looked like I'd been pushed
to the point of taking my own life,

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:12.520
I'd finally be able to quit.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:15.520
So I agreed to do it...

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.270
I'm sorry.

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:19.560
You should've just told us.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:21.850
I'm sure you would've been able to say it.

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:26.940
But I... I didn't want to be the bad guy.

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:29.270
I didn't want everyone to hate me.

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:33.440
It's not like I want people to hate me, either.

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:35.730
You're right. I'm sorry.

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:40.400
Well, I'll get going.

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:45.310
Take care. Don't push yourself too hard.

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:46.940
Yeah...

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.230
Chika...

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:55.150
You're actually a genius, so you may
never be pushed to the edge like I was...

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:58.810
But if you ever feel betrayed by volleyball,

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:02.480
I think it might hit you pretty hard.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:05.900
So I am pretty worried about that.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:12.900
So were you guys able to talk?

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:14.310
Yeah.

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:16.600
And did anything change?

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:20.650
Who knows? But I got some closure.

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:23.270
I see. Well, that's good.

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:27.520
So what possessed you to go
to Tokyo in that state?

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:30.400
I didn't think I actually had a fever.

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:33.350
But you should've known
if you felt lethargic or not.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:34.810
You need to rest.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.350
But I can't deal with it.

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:41.150
If even a day goes by where
I don't play volleyball... I panic.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:45.020
I guess you are sorta reckless.

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:46.940
Mr. Haijima.

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:49.060
Someone's here to get you.

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:50.440
Hello.

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:55.940
Well? How are you feeling?

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:57.520
Ms. Minami!

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:01.650
I-It's been so long!

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:06.520
You've gotten taller, Chika.

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:10.650
You were a volleyball player, too?

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:15.850
Yes. I was on a team for work,
but I quit that, and now I'm a teacher.

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:20.150
Chika, do you feel all right?
You can lay down if you need to.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:21.980
No, I'm okay.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:24.520
Yeah, I totally get it now.

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.810
I mean, she wasn't actually Vabo- <i>chan</i> ,

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:29.310
but maybe I should've
caught a ride somewhere else.

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:30.690
The hell are you talking about?

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:34.650
The girl you said you like is her, isn't it?

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:38.690
Man, I guess you can be normal.

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.650
Ow! Hey!

00:13:41.650 --> 00:13:45.810
Hey, back there. It's a small car
so stop the roughhousing.

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:49.270
Hey, I just saw the word "Shinjuku"!

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:50.150
Did you want to go?

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:51.310
Can we?!

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:54.850
Learn how to say no, damn it!
She's nice enough to take us to the station.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:59.520
What? I wanted to look around
Tokyo at least a little bit.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.100
I mean, since we're here...

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:08.060
Ms. Minami. Sorry, could you
stop here for a bit?

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:09.310
You got it.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:16.810
Let's go see the best thing in Tokyo.

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:23.020
The Tokyo Metropolitan Gymnasium.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.310
This is where the Spring Tournament is.

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:27.020
So this is...

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:31.060
I've come here so many times
ever since I started playing.

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:35.150
On the days of the tournament,
there's a huge Vabo- <i>chan</i> balloon.

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:38.400
There're lots of spectators
and enthusiastic cheer squads.

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.350
Cheerleaders and brass bands...

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:42.480
Reporters and TV cameras...

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:46.350
And the teams representing their prefectures.

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:50.730
From the semi-finals, the games
are played on the center court.

00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:55.190
The only ones able to stand there
are the best teams and players

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:57.690
who actually have a shot
at becoming the best in Japan.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.520
Okay, I get it.

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:04.600
The place is great, I get it. And I get
why you want to come here so bad.

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:07.650
And I know that you're a setter worthy enough

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:09.350
to stand in the middle of that court.

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:13.520
This isn't about me.

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:16.060
You need to imagine standing there yourself.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.810
Actually want that for once.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:22.560
Once you play against the best players
there, you'll want it even more!

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:25.770
You'll want to get even stronger
and want more time!

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:29.690
That's why I want you to be the ace...

00:15:32.020 --> 00:15:33.350
Ms. Minami.

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:36.900
I know I said that I would make it
to the Spring Tournament with Meisei...

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.770
Sorry, I have to take that back.

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:40.850
I want to get there with Seiin.

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:44.650
I want to get here with them now.

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:46.940
You don't need to apologize.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:52.730
Sota came to me almost in tears
asking if he could quit volleyball, too.

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:55.480
You're all in high school now.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:16:00.440
It's only natural for your friends
and interests to change.

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:04.810
That's how much time you all spent together.

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.600
You talked to Sota, too?

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.150
Yes.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.690
I'm really sorry...

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:13.980
I just told you that you
don't need to apologize.

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:17.560
You're the one who got hurt
in all of this, Chika.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:21.150
We're sorry, too.

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:26.230
Ms. Minami... I'm okay now.
Because I didn't come here alone.

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:28.270
So I'll be okay.

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:29.770
I see.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:33.150
I guess it was good that
you went to Seiin High after all.

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:36.980
You know about Seiin, ma'am?

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:40.520
Who do you think had me go
all the way to the hospital to pick you up?

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:43.650
The coach from Meisei Middle School
asked me to get you.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:45.100
The coach...?

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:48.940
Apparently, he felt responsible
about you transferring.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:52.150
He figured all this would die down
once you entered high school,

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:55.440
so he was thinking about
bringing you back to Meisei,

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:57.810
but he decided against it.

00:16:57.810 --> 00:16:59.730
Why?

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:02.980
Because the Seiin High's volleyball team...

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:05.480
...has a famous coach.

00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:08.480
Famous coach?!

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.690
So there you have it.

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:14.020
Adults have some connections that
you kids just don't understand yet.

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:20.310
Just how much trouble
are you two going to cause for us?!

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:22.940
S-Sorry...

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:25.810
So about the prefectural qualifiers...

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.560
We'll be able to enter.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:28.980
Really?

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.400
Yeah. Someone spoke up for Kuroba.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:33.560
Was it...

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:35.480
It's Kuroba's cousin...

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:37.480
Itoko.

00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:40.400
Yuni Kuroba has a bruise
on his face because I hit him!

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:42.440
He teased me, so I lost my temper!

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:46.310
I had no idea that the
volleyball team was suspended!

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:48.150
So that's that.

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:51.310
Why the hell would you keep
something like that a secret?

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:53.900
Well, then Itoko would have to apologize.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:57.060
Is that the only reason you didn't say anything?

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:01.810
Go home!

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:04.020
Yeah, that's it.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:06.770
All right. I'll accept that.

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:09.520
By the way, Haijima, how are you feeling?

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.480
I'm good.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:14.310
The prefectural qualifiers start
at the end of September.

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:17.690
We've only got a month, but I haven't given up.

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:20.150
See what you want to do through to the end.

00:18:20.150 --> 00:18:22.980
We'll back you up even if
our lives depend on it.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:24.810
We won't leave you all alone.

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:28.350
Right. I'll make sure we make it in time.

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:37.810
Oda- <i>senpai</i> , I'm sorry that my careless
actions caused us so much trouble.

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:40.730
Senpai, I want to go to the Spring Tournament.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:46.350
I want to go there with everyone
and hit a spike on that center court.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:47.480
Yeah.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:53.690
I want to see the same thing
as Haijima does, and just as clearly.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:58.480
I'm sure you know this already,
but this guy's super greedy.

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:04.810
He's called a genius setter, has a lot
of talent, and he's still not satisfied.

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:07.600
He still wants so much more.

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:11.440
And this is the one thing he wants
so badly that his eyes even sparkle!

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:16.560
It must be some kind of awesome treasure!

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:18.600
Don't worry, you're getting through to us.

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:23.020
We hear you loud and clear and
we know you were thinking about us.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:34.440
Well, see you at practice
tomorrow morning, Senpai.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:55.480
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:19:57.100 --> 00:20:02.730
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:11.560
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:15.600
<i>The azure world smiles upon me</i>

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:27.940
<i>The knife made up of words from my friend</i>

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:34.850
<i>Still lingers inside my head today</i>

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:41.060
<i>You glared up at the clouds high in the sky</i>

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:47.520
<i>And near your house, the horizon undulated</i>

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:54.980
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:20:56.600 --> 00:21:02.100
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:21:03.850 --> 00:21:11.020
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:19.190
<i>The azure world stabs me strongly in the back</i>

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:32.980
Heya.

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:33.810
Hey.

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:36.810
Is that really what you guys
are having for breakfast?

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:38.480
They finally lifted our suspension

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:42.900
so we're prepared to spend
the rest of our time practicing.

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:43.850
Yeah.

00:21:43.850 --> 00:21:48.350
So, the third years showed up
followed by the second years.

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:51.400
The first years have the balls to show up late?

00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:55.520
What are you talking about, Aoki?
We weren't the first ones here.

00:21:57.350 --> 00:22:00.350
Haijima, I'm just gonna say one thing.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:02.600
I'm way greedier than you are.

00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:08.810
I get to have an amazing setter like you,
and I want everything that you want.

00:22:08.810 --> 00:22:14.020
On top of that, I wanna be your ace,
so I'm the greediest one here.

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:19.940
You know... You wanting my talent
and everything I want is a lot.

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:22.310
You better be prepared
if you actually want all of that.

00:22:22.310 --> 00:22:24.980
I'm going to climb even higher.

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:27.850
You seriously say stuff like that.

00:22:27.850 --> 00:22:30.560
First, we have to get through
the prefectural qualifiers.

00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:34.770
We're gonna smash Fukuho Technical
High School's record for being the reps.

00:22:34.770 --> 00:22:37.440
We don't have time to waste at that level.

00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:39.230
We don't have time. Let's go.

00:22:39.230 --> 00:22:40.230
Yeah.

00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:42.350
Let's go!

00:22:42.350 --> 00:22:43.400
Yeah!

00:22:46.560 --> 00:22:49.730
Kuroba... we can make it.

00:22:56.310 --> 00:22:59.440
This team can make it...

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:00.770
...to the Spring Tournament.
